# How to cite Homeo.  GitHub shows it as "Cite this repository"; Zenodo
# reads it for the archived release's record.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Homeo, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Homeo: a simulation of Ashby's homeostat and of homeostat-controlled robots"
abstract: >-
  A software simulation of W. Ross Ashby's homeostat, as described in Design
  for a Brain and An Introduction to Cybernetics, and a platform for research
  with it: Ashby's own experiments, generalized homeostatic units and
  uniselectors, and homeostats as the controllers of simulated robots
  (Braitenberg vehicles) in a built-in Box2D simulator or in Webots, with
  genetic algorithms that evolve them.
authors:
  - family-names: Franchi
    given-names: Stefano
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6955-6320"
version: 0.1.0
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/cleinias/Homeo"
keywords:
  - homeostat
  - W. Ross Ashby
  - cybernetics
  - ultrastability
  - homeostasis
  - Braitenberg vehicles
  - simulation
